# The three NeoForge block capabilities every tech mod is built on. Shipped from the loader module
# rather than from :stagewright-api because the api compiles against neither loader — which is also
# why Fabric has no counterpart file: it has no platform energy standard to wrap, and a scene asking
# for 'energy' there gets a skip that says so.
#
# This file and the api's must MERGE into the shadow jar, not replace one another. Shadow's default
# is last-writer-wins per path, so `mergeServiceFiles()` in neoforge/build.gradle is load-bearing:
# without it the jar ships one of the two and every capability in the other reports itself absent,
# which reads exactly like an uninstalled mod.
net.magicterra.stagewright.neoforge.caps.BlockEnergy$Provider
net.magicterra.stagewright.neoforge.caps.BlockFluids$Provider
net.magicterra.stagewright.neoforge.caps.BlockItems$Provider
